    "Politics",
    "Fliers"
  ],
  "strategy": "Ms. Bumbleflower hands an opponent a card on every spell you cast, puts a +1/+1 counter and flying on a creature, and draws you two on the second spell of a turn, so the deck plays a stream of cheap spells and wins in the air with whatever it grew. Rites of Flourishing, Kwain, Selvala, Intellectual Offering, Tempt with Bunnies and Tempt with Discovery share cards, lands and life with the table, and Jolly Gerbils, Long River's Pull, Peerless Recycling, Wear Down and Octomancer turn each gift into value of your own. Psychosis Crawler, Body of Knowledge and Twenty-Toed Toad cash in the full hands, the Toad winning outright with twenty cards in hand, while Baird, Tenuous Truce, Riot Control and Illusionist's Gambit keep the gifted opponents pointed somewhere else.",
